  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Central Asia Regional Economic Coperation Corridor 2 (Bukhara-Miskin-Urgench-Khiva) Railway Electrification Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will add electrification, signaling and telecommunication, and traction power management systems to the recently built railway line between Bukhara, Miskin, Urgench, and Khiva, a total of 465 km. The line has a design speed of 250 km per hour and connects to the electrified high-speed railway line between the country?s capital Tashkent, Samarkand, and Bukhara.</narrative>
  </description>
